==Enemy==
Kory, despite his lowish range, damage and speed, has the ability to create a Level 4 [[Wave Attack]] that reaches up to 1067.5 range. He is fairly tough for how early he is encountered, having many knockbacks but also lots of health making him difficult to take down, especially when supporting other enemies.

==Strategy==
Like most [[:Category:Wave Attack Enemies|Wave Attackers]], Kory fires off waves that near-completely invalidate the use of meatshields and tanks since they'll hit pretty much everything, and using them will only lead to him generating more waves. Much like [[Mr. Mole]], he can quickly destroy more fragile stackable attackers, so they too are ineffective.

In early- to mid-[[Stories of Legend]], Kory is best dealt with durable melee units such as [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]] and [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]]. Ideally, these units should be decently disposable and have few knockbacks, so they can get consistent hits on Kory if other threats don't get in the way. Rushers that do lots of damage quickly like [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] can be helpful later on, using Kory's knockbacks to their advantage when protected properly.

Another option is using powerful midrangers or such as [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] and refrain from sending out other units, hoping that they cause enough damage to stagger Kory at range before he has a chance to hit them. Backliners and others stand no chance, as the waves will keep them from having any impact, unless they are immune/resistant or you employ [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shields]]. [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] is the most accessible option, but a few others, while difficult to obtain, can outrange Kory while still negating his waves. [[:Category:Cats with Wave Immunity|Wave-immune units]] are of course good to bring, as they completely ignore his wave.

There are not many accessible units that can deal with Kory efficiently due to Kory's Traitless typing. Some great counters include [[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Lord of Ruin Jagando Jr.]] and [[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]], especially when Kory becomes too tanky to ward off with damage alone, although [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Glass Cat]] and [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Vendor Cat and Kitten]] can be effective for their status effects that delay Kory from pushing. [[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] units and [[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Demon Cat]] are good to bring if you have them.

Later in the game, Kory will become much less threatening, specifically when you get Octopus Cat and [[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Mightycat]]. His spotlight and notoriety as a common yet nasty waver will be stolen by his angrier counterpart, [[Berserkory]].

