==Existence Elsewhere==
===Nyanko Defense Force===
In [[Nyanko Defence Force]], Kory had many new variants that could be fought as Raid Bosses. They had two attacks: they could summon a cascade of falling icicles from the top of the screen, and they could shoot giant icicles from their hatchets, which would then split into six smaller projectiles. Some units had an ability called Kory Killer, which increased damage against all Kory variants by 50%.

{{Gallery|Enemy icon 034}}

==Trivia==
*Kory's Japanese name, Koalakkyo (コアラッキョ ''Koarakkyo''), may be derived from ''koala'' and 別居 ''bekkyo'' (living separately), 独居 ''dokkyo'' (living alone), or 雑居 ''zakkyo'' (living together), referring to how he lives with [[Gory]] until he is kicked out. It may also involve スラック ''surakku'' (slack) or the Internet slang term 絶許 ''zekkyo'' (short for 絶対に許せない ''zettai ni yurusenai'', "it's absolutely unforgivable").
*[[Three Evil Brothers]] implies that Kory, [[Berserkory]] and [[Koronium]] are brothers.
*Kory is the first character in the game to have [[Wave Attack]]s.
**In terms of ID, Kory is also the first character to have Base Destroyer, but not the first to appear in-game: [[Camelle]] is encountered earlier and was added in the same update in spite of having a higher ID.
*In [[Nyanko Defence Force]], Kory was the only boss to lack a non-Raid variant.
**Since the Frozen Kory Raid Boss was the first Kory added to the game, he was used as the base for all the others, hence why even the fire variants used icicles to attack.

